<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''Root-Cartographer: Lares (Tasked Spirit)''

The strongest first move is to give the existing private projection tree a separately mounted root outside the container’s reset target. The memory-stage working mirror, content-keyed rows, ingest-back, and kāpae shadows already provide much of the content migration path. They do not yet make a complete backup or prove that every possible memory row round-trips.

The checkout is on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`. This was a read-only code inspection; I ran no tests or vessel.

* ''BENDS — the proposed house layout.'' With `LAR_ROOT` set, the actual tree is `<root>/data/lares/{vessel,identity,nexus}`, `<root>/data/lararium/sensoriums/...`, `<root>/{state,cache,config,run}`, plus projection `bags/` and `wikis/`. Without it, the data, state, cache, config and runtime resolvers use their respective XDG homes; `~/.lares` is separately used as the vessel home. The repeated `lares` distinguishes the spirits’ data from the lararium’s data; `state` identifies both an outer container mount in the brief and an inner XDG facet. A `hearth/projections/indexes` layout therefore needs resolver and caller changes, not just directory renames. [[vessel-paths.ts:66|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-paths.ts:66]], [[vessel-paths.ts:120|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-paths.ts:120]], [[xdg-base.ts:29|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mempalace/src/xdg-base.ts:29]].

* ''BREAKS — classify all sensoriums as rebuildable indexes.'' The resolver explicitly describes lararium capture as potentially unique and not rebuildable; memory also includes structure, form and persistence, not merely a vector index. Classify each plane against its actual surviving inputs before moving it into disposable `indexes/`. [[xdg-base.ts:35|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mempalace/src/xdg-base.ts:35]], [[vessel-paths.ts:274|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-paths.ts:274]].

* ''HOLDS — projections outside the wipe boundary, with changes.'' `projectionRoots` sends canon-sourced bags and their wikis back to their source; other bags go under the state root. Private daemon-working and kahua-stage mirrors also take that root directly. Add an explicit private projection root and thread it through //all// these grants, preserving the canon-origin split. Merely changing `projectionRoots` misses the private mirrors and the per-wiki grant bases. [[bag-paths.ts:141|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:141]], [[bag-paths.ts:245|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:245]], [[open-node-vessel.ts:4036|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4036]]. ''Inference:'' a sibling host directory needs its own container bind or another explicitly exposed location; a sibling inside `/state` still gets cleared.

* ''BENDS — the two mounts and reset.'' Compose binds `LARES_STATE` to `/state` and `LARES_WORKSPACE` to `/workspace`; canon bags and wikis use the latter. The existing container `reset` already refuses a running vessel, requires a terminal, resolves paths, checks several unsafe overlaps and running bind holders, and asks for `re-found`. It removes ''every entry'' in `LARES_STATE`, not just an inner `hearth/`, and does not perform the proposed coverage, staging, conflict or export checks. A root split must change both mount and reset contracts. [[docker-compose.surface.yml:138|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/docker-compose.surface.yml:138]], [[lares-container.sh:223|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/tools/lares-container.sh:223]].

* ''ALREADY BUILT under another name — memory-stage projection.'' The daemon working mirror already projects to `wikis/kahua-<face relation>` and the kahua stage to `bags/kahua-<face relation>` under the private root. `meme_put` requires an explicit recipe or bag; `recipe="default"` names the daemon wiki. The control-plane `bags/daemon` is deliberately unmirrored, so enabling a generic “daemon memory bag” would conflate distinct surfaces. The survival problem is their current placement inside reset, not an absent working mirror. [[bag-paths.ts:158|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:158]], [[lares_mcp.py:118|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/lares_mcp.py:118]].

* ''BENDS — temp and draft projection with cleanup.'' A recipe-designated draft recovery grant, its own directory, store subscription, startup scan and at-rest check already exist; it is not universally enabled. Temp needs its own explicit design, especially because the projector describes the volatile plane as never persisted or stamped. Automatic cleanup must retain the operator’s deliberate projection choice and protect edited or sole copies. The founding road asks for temp and draft behind a flag with automated cleanup. [[open-node-vessel.ts:4064|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4064]], [[disk-projector.ts:490|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:490]], [[stable-founding-road.mem:160|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:160]].

* ''BREAKS — include drafts in the memory-stage re-pour as proposed.'' The current stage ruling says exports and re-pours carry the ''working layer and its kāpae'', never drafts; upper-layer work is not a stage row until the working seam. Draft recovery projection can exist separately, but treating it as stage migration needs an amended ruling. [[stable-founding-road.mem:382|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:382]].

* ''ALREADY BUILT under another name — much of import.'' `lares vessel seed` discovers holdings; system bags use diff-gated ingest, while other holdings use CREATE → LOAD to working → MOVE to canon. It previews by default and processes holdings sequentially, continuing after failures: it is not an atomic bundle import. `lares ingest --in-wiki` already provides working-layer ingest-back, with preview, hashes and an explicit target bag. Its address derivation depends on the configured bags/wikis roots, so an arbitrary export directory is not automatically an import source. [[seed.ts:53|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lares-cli/src/commands/seed.ts:53]], [[seed.ts:87|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lares-cli/src/commands/seed.ts:87]], [[ingest.ts:30|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lares-cli/src/commands/ingest.ts:30]], [[ingest-core.ts:153|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:153]].

* ''ALREADY BUILT under another name — durable exclusions and keyed re-pour.'' `.kapae` carries a raised exclusion by title and layer location; ingest checks that its title agrees with its siting and raises it again. Memory-stage `row-key` deterministically fixes the title, and an existing test pours one exported example into two fresh sinks and compares its fields and text. This is a content re-pour, not restoration of old authority or history. [[kapae-shadow.ts:1|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/kapae-shadow.ts:1]], [[ingest-core.ts:192|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:192]], [[place-meme.ts:254|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/place-meme.ts:254]], [[place-meme.test.ts:273|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/tests/place-meme.test.ts:273]].

* ''BENDS — “`.mem` round-trips every memory-row field.”'' The tested keyed example does round-trip. Authored fields, including `row-key` and `lar_*`, can travel in TOML; structural fields are reconstructed. But the renderer deliberately omits `modified`, `revision`, `file-path`, handle internals, `$` fields and empty values, and skinny pointers can use a different representation. Therefore a blanket //every field// claim is false; which omitted fields a real memory row requires remains to be demonstrated with a representative fixture. [[deserializer.ts:780|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/deserializer.ts:780]], [[deserializer.ts:881|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/deserializer.ts:881]], [[meme-write.ts:109|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-write.ts:109]].

* ''BENDS — verified export and conflict handling.'' The projector already queues by carrier, compares disk, base and rendered hashes, surfaces divergent edits without overwriting, and has an idle handshake. It writes a same-directory temporary file and renames it, but the shown implementation does not fsync; those per-file mechanics do not establish a consistent multi-bag snapshot. A manifest, coverage report, barrier or equivalent snapshot, and explicit concurrent-value handling remain design work. [[disk-projector.ts:44|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:44]], [[disk-projector.ts:602|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:602]], [[disk-projector.ts:1217|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:1217]]. Saves without a booked session can wait in memory, so reset cannot infer durable coverage merely from projection files. [[open-node-vessel.ts:905|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:905]].

The smallest first lane should extend [[projection-roots-split.test.ts|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/tests/projection-roots-split.test.ts:30]], then change [[bag-paths.ts|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:255]], [[open-node-vessel.ts|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4036]], the daemon mirror wiring, [[docker-compose.surface.yml|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/docker-compose.surface.yml:138]], and [[lares-container.sh|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/tools/lares-container.sh:223]]. The red test should configure distinct state, workspace and private-projection roots and assert that a house bag, daemon working mirror and kahua stage resolve outside state, while a sourced bag still resolves to workspace. A companion container/reset test should prove the projection bind survives clearing state. This proves the new boundary, not end-to-end recovery; the lead should run any socket-dependent re-found witness.

The research’s principal factual errors were assuming memory projection had to be invented, treating all sensoriums as rebuildable, overlooking the existing draft recovery and kāpae paths, treating `~/.lares` as the universal resolver default, and proposing draft stage re-pours contrary to the current ruling. The reports also treated conflict gates and keyed re-pour as prospective when substantial pieces already exist. Full identity continuity, face bundles, emergency recovery and backup restore remain deferred by the founding road. [[stable-founding-road.mem:160|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:160]].

<<~/ahu>>

